<span class="section-num">4.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 4</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְעַל-כֵּן צְרִיכִין לְהַקְדִּים בְּנוֹ לְבֶן בְּנוֹ. וּבֶן בְּנוֹ לְבֶן חֲבֵרוֹ, כִּי צְרִיכִין לְהָאִיר הַנְּקֻדָּה בְּבָנָיו יוֹתֵר מֵחֲמַת שֶׁבָּנָיו נִמְשְׁכוּ מִמֶּנּוּ, וְכָל נְקֻדָּתָם הַקְּדוֹשָׁה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בָּהֶם נִמְשָׁךְ מִמֶּנּוּ. כִּי עִקַּר הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּכָל אֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל הוּא מֵחֲמַת שֶׁהוּא מִזֶּרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי כָּל אֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל יֵשׁ בּוֹ נְקֻדָּה קְדוֹשָׁה מִצַּד הוּלַּדְתּוֹ מֵחֲמַת שֶׁהוּא מִזֶּרַע אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב, כִּי אַבְרָהָם זָכָה לָזֶה לְהַמְשִׁיךְ אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה לוֹ וּלְזַרְעוֹ אַחֲרָיו לְדוֹרוֹת עוֹלָם, כִּי מִמֶּנּוּ הִתְחִיל שַׁלְשֶׁלֶת הַיּוֹחֲסִין שֶׁל קְדֻשַּׁת יִשְׂרָאֵל שֶׁלֹּא תִּפָּסֵק לְעוֹלָם, כִּי מֵאַבְרָהָם נִמְשְׁכָה הַנְּקֻדָּה מִצַּד הַהוֹלָדָה לְיִצְחָק בְּנוֹ שֶׁרַק הוּא נִקְרָא זַרְעוֹ, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, בְּיִצְחָק יִקָּרֵא לְךָ זֶרַע. וְכֵן מִיִּצְחָק לְיַעֲקֹב. וְיַעֲקֹב הָיָה מִטָּתוֹ שְׁלֵמָה וּמִמֶּנּוּ נִמְשְׁכָה הַנְּקֻדָּה בִּשְׁלֵמוּת לִשְׁנֵים עָשָׂר שִׁבְטֵי יָהּ וְכֵן מִדּוֹר לְדוֹר לְעוֹלָם שֶׁכָּל אֶחָד וְאֶחָד מִזֶּרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יֵשׁ בּוֹ נְקֻדָּה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה מֵחֲמַת הַהוֹלָדָה מֵחֲמַת שֶׁהוּא מִזֶּרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל מִזֶּרַע אַבְרָהָם יִצְחָק וְיַעֲקֹב, כִּי עִקַּר הַנְּקֻדָּה הִיא בִּבְחִינַת בְּרִית, בְּחִינַת צַדִּיק יְסוֹד עוֹלָם, כְּמוֹ שֶׁמְּבֹאָר שָׁם בְּהַתּוֹרָה הַנַּ"ל. וּמִשָּׁם כָּל הַהוֹלָדוֹת, כִּי הוּא צִנּוֹר שֶׁל כָּל הַנְּשָׁמוֹת כַּיָּדוּעַ וְכָל יִשְׂרָאֵל עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהֵם נִמּוֹלִים הֵם כֻּלָּם בִּבְחִינַת קְדֻשַּׁת הַבְּרִית, ((כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתַב רַבֵּנוּ זַ"ל בְּמָקוֹם אַחֵר בְּסִימָן כג) בִּבְחִינַת צַדִּיקִים, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, וְעַמֵּךְ כֻּלָּם צַדִּיקִים. וְזֶה זָכוּ מֵאַבְרָהָם שֶׁהָיָה רֹאשׁ לַנִּמּוֹלִים וְהוּא הָרִאשׁוֹן שֶׁהֶעֱבִיר הַחֶרְפָּה שֶׁהִיא הָעָרְלָה דְּחַפְיָא עַל בְּרִית. שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה הֵאִיר אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁהִיא בְּחִינַת צַדִּיק יְסוֹד עוֹלָם וְזָכָה לְהוֹלִיד אֶת יִצְחָק אַחֲרֵי שֶׁכְּבָר הָיָה נִמּוֹל וְעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה זָכָה לְהוֹרִישׁ קְדֻשַּׁת יִשְׂרָאֵל לְדוֹרוֹת שֶׁכָּל זַרְעוֹ שֶׁהֵם זֶרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל יַמְשִׁיכוּ הַנְּקֻדָּה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה מֵאָב לְבֵן מִדּוֹר לְדוֹר לְעוֹלָם כַּנַּ"ל: נִמְצָא, שֶׁהַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁל כָּל אֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל הִוא נִמְשֶׁכֶת מֵאָבִיו מִצַּד הַהוֹלָדָה כַּנַּ"ל, אֲבָל מֵחֲמַת זֻהֲמַת הַנָּחָשׁ שֶׁהוּא הִתְגַּבְּרוּת הַתַּאֲוֹת שֶׁנִּמְשָׁכִין מִשְּׁבִירַת כֵּלִים מֵהַחֲרָפוֹת הַנַּ"ל עַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נִתְעַלֵּם וְנִסְתָּר אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּכָל אֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל מִצַּד הַהוֹלָדָה, כִּי הַחֲרָפוֹת לֵב שְׁבִירַת לֵב הֵם מִתְגַּבְּרִים בְּהַהוֹלָדָה דַּיְקָא, כִּי זֶה כְּלָל שֶׁבְּמָקוֹם שֶׁהַקְּדֻשָּׁה גָּבֹהַּ יוֹתֵר שָׁם הֵם מִתְגַּבְּרִים בְּיוֹתֵר, כִּי אֶת זֶה לְעֻמַּת זֶה עָשָׂה אֱלֹקִים וְכוּ'. וְעַל-כֵּן בְּרֹב הַהוֹלָדוֹת נֶאֱחָז בָּהֶם בְּחִינַת שְׁבִירַת לֵב חֶרְפַּת לֵב שֶׁמֵּהֶם הַקְּלִפָּה הַחוֹפָה עַל הַפְּרִי שֶׁמֵּהֶם כָּל הַתַּאֲוֹת שֶׁעַל יָדָם נִתְעַלֵּם אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה. וְזֶה כָּל הָעֲבוֹדָה שֶׁל כָּל אָדָם לְהִתְגַּבֵּר לְהָאִיר עֶצֶם הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בּוֹ שֶׁתָּאִיר לְלִבּוֹ עַל-יְדֵי הַדִּבּוּר שֶׁמְּדַבֵּר בֵּינוֹ לְבֵין קוֹנוֹ וְעִם חֲבֵרָיו וְרַבּוֹ וְכוּ' כַּנַּ"ל. כְּדֵי לְבַטֵּל בְּחִינַת הַחֶרְפָּה הַשּׁוֹרָה עַל לִבּוֹ שֶׁנִּמְשֶׁכֶת מִשְּׁבִירַת כֵּלִים מֵחֲמַת שֶׁלֹּא נִתְקַדֵּשׁ אָבִיו בִּשְׁעַת הַהוֹלָדָה. וְעַל-כֵּן הַחִיּוּב מֻטָּל עַל אָבִיו בְּיוֹתֵר לְדַבֵּר עִם בְּנוֹ בְּתוֹרָה וְיִרְאַת שָׁמַיִם כְּדֵי לְהָאִיר בּוֹ הַנְּקֻדָּה מִפֶּה לַלֵּב כַּנַּ"ל. כִּי עַל אָבִיו דַּיְקָא מֻטָּל הַחִיּוּב בְּיוֹתֵר מֵחֲמַת שֶׁעֶצֶם הַנְּקֻדָּה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה נִמְשְׁכָה מִמֶּנּוּ מֵחֲמַת שֶׁהוּא מִזֶּרַע יִשְׂרָאֵל כַּנַּ"ל. וְגַם הַחֶרְפָּה הַשּׁוֹרָה עַל לִבּוֹ הִוא גַּם כֵּן עַל יָדוֹ עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁלֹּא קִדֵּשׁ עַצְמוֹ כָּרָאוּי. וְעַל-כֵּן הוּא מְחֻיָּב לִלְמֹד עִם בְּנוֹ תּוֹרָה שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה מְתַקֵּן כָּל זֹאת, כִּי עַל-יְדֵי שֶׁהוּא לוֹמֵד עִם בְּנוֹ הוּא מֵאִיר בּוֹ הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בּוֹ מִקְּדֻשַּׁת יִשְׂרָאֵל וּמְבַטֵּל הַחֶרְפָּה הַשּׁוֹרָה עַל לֵב, כִּי הַכֹּל נִמְשָׁךְ מֵאָבִיו וְהוּא צָרִיךְ לְתַקֵּן כָּל זֶה עַל-יְדֵי הַדִּבּוּר שֶׁמְּדַבֵּר עִם בְּנוֹ בְּתוֹרָה וְיִרְאַת שָׁמַיִם. שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה מְאִירָה הַנְּקֻדָּה מִפֶּה לַלֵּב שֶׁעַל-יְדֵי-זֶה נִתְתַּקֵּן הַכֹּל וְכַנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And therefore one must give <strong>precedence to his son</strong> over his grandson, and his grandson over the son of his fellow. For one must illuminate the <em>nekudah</em> in his sons more — because his sons were drawn from him, and their entire holy <em>nekudah</em> is drawn from him. For the primary <em>nekudah</em> in every Jew is because he is of the seed of Israel. For every Jew has a holy <em>nekudah</em> by virtue of his birth — because he is of the seed of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov. For Avraham merited this: to draw the light of the holy <em>nekudah</em> for himself and his descendants after him for all generations. For from him began the <strong>chain of lineage (<em>shalsheles hayuchasin</em>)</strong> of the holiness of Israel, which will never be broken.</p>

<p>For from Avraham the <em>nekudah</em> was drawn through birth to Yitzchak his son — for only he is called his seed, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"Through Yitzchak shall your seed be called"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Genesis 21:12)</span>. And similarly from Yitzchak to Yaakov. And Yaakov — his bed was complete, and from him the <em>nekudah</em> was drawn in completeness to the twelve tribes of Y-ah. And so from generation to generation forever — every single person of the seed of Israel has the holy <em>nekudah</em> through birth, because he is of the seed of Israel, of the seed of Avraham, Yitzchak, and Yaakov. For the primary <em>nekudah</em> is in the aspect of the <em>bris</em>, the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"a <em>tzadik</em> is the foundation of the world"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Proverbs 10:25)</span>, as is explained there in the aforementioned Torah. And from there are all births — for it is the channel of all <em>neshamos</em>, as is known. And all Israel, through being circumcised, are all in the aspect of the holiness of the <em>bris</em> (as Rabbeinu of blessed memory wrote elsewhere, in Torah 23) — in the aspect of <em>tzadikim</em>, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"And your people are all <em>tzadikim</em>"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Isaiah 60:21)</span>. And this they merited from Avraham, who was the head of the circumcised — and he was the first to remove the <em>cherpah</em>, which is the <em>orlah</em> that covers the <em>bris</em>. Through which he illuminated the light of the <em>nekudah</em>, which is the aspect of <span class="verse-inline">"a <em>tzadik</em> is the foundation of the world,"</span> and merited giving birth to Yitzchak after he was already circumcised. And through this he merited bequeathing the holiness of Israel for all generations — that all his descendants, who are the seed of Israel, would draw the holy <em>nekudah</em> from father to son, from generation to generation forever, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>It turns out that the <em>nekudah</em> of every single Jew is drawn from his father by virtue of birth, as mentioned above. But because of the <strong>contamination of the serpent (<em>zuhamas hanachash</em>)</strong> — which is the intensification of the desires drawn from the <em>sh'viras keilim</em>, from the aforementioned <em>charafos</em> — through this the light of the <em>nekudah</em> that is in every Jew from birth becomes hidden and concealed. For the <em>charafos lev</em>, the <em>sh'viras lev</em>, intensify specifically at birth — for this is a general principle: wherever the <em>kedushah</em> is higher, there they intensify more, for <span class="verse-inline">"G-d made this corresponding to that"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Ecclesiastes 7:14)</span> etc. And therefore in most births, the aspect of <em>sh'viras lev</em>, <em>cherpas lev</em>, clings to them — from which is the <em>klipah</em> that covers the fruit, from which are all the desires through which the light of the <em>nekudah</em> is hidden.</p>

<p>And this is the entire service of every person: to strive to illuminate the essential <em>nekudah</em> that is in him — that it should illuminate to his heart — through speech, speaking between himself and his Creator and with his friends and his Rav etc., as mentioned above. In order to nullify the aspect of the <em>cherpah</em> that rests upon his heart, which is drawn from the <em>sh'viras keilim</em> — because his father did not sanctify himself at the time of birth. And therefore the obligation rests upon <strong>his father</strong> most of all — to speak with his son in Torah and <em>yiras shamayim</em>, in order to illuminate in him the <em>nekudah</em> from mouth to heart, as mentioned above. For upon his father specifically the obligation rests most — because the essential holy <em>nekudah</em> was drawn from him, since he is of the seed of Israel, as mentioned above. And also the <em>cherpah</em> that rests upon his heart is also through him — through not having sanctified himself properly. And therefore he is obligated to learn Torah with his son — through which all this is rectified. For through learning with his son, he illuminates in him the <em>nekudah</em> that is in him from the holiness of Israel, and nullifies the <em>cherpah</em> that rests upon the heart. For everything is drawn from his father — and he must rectify all this through the speech that he speaks with his son in Torah and <em>yiras shamayim</em>, through which the <em>nekudah</em> illuminates from mouth to heart, through which everything is rectified, as mentioned above.</p>

