<span class="section-num">5.</span>
<button class="hebrew-toggle" onclick="this.nextElementSibling.classList.toggle('visible')">☰ Hebrew § 5</button>
<div class="hebrew-block">וְזֶה בְּחִינַת קְרִיאַת שְׁמַע. שְׁמַע יִשְׂרָאֵל ה' אֱלֹקֵינוּ ה' אֶחָד, זֶה בְּחִינַת אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה שֶׁיֵּשׁ בְּכָל אֶחָד מִיִּשְׂרָאֵל, כִּי עִקַּר קְדֻשַּׁת הַנְּקֻדָּה הִיא הָאֱמוּנָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה שֶׁהִיא יְסוֹד הַכֹּל, כִּי הָאֱמוּנָה הִיא עִקַּר הַקְּדֻשָּׁה כְּלַל כָּל הַתּוֹרָה, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, כָּל מִצְוֹתֶיךָ אֱמוּנָה. וְהִיא עִקַּר הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁל בְּחִינַת צַדִּיק, כְּמוֹ שֶׁכָּתוּב, וְצַדִּיק בֶּאֱמוּנָתוֹ יִחְיֶה. וְאָנוּ צְרִיכִין לוֹמַר קְרִיאַת שְׁמַע בְּפֶה מָלֵא דַּיְקָא, כִּי עִקַּר אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה נִתְגַּלֶּה עַל-יְדֵי דִּבּוּר פֶּה דַּיְקָא כַּנַּ"ל. וְזֶהוּ, וְאָהַבְתָּ אֶת ה' אֱלֹקֶיךָ וְכוּ'.. 'וְאָהַבְתָּ' זֶה בְּחִינַת אוֹר הָאַהֲבָה הַקְּדוֹשָׁה שֶׁשּׁוֹרָה אֵצֶל הַנְּקֻדָּה כַּנַּ"ל. וְזֶהוּ, וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל לְבָבֶךָ. 'עַל לְבָבֶךָ' דַּיְקָא, כִּי צָרִיךְ לְקַשֵּׁר וּלְהָאִיר הַנְּקֻדָּה מִפֶּה לַלֵּב כַּנַּ"ל. וְהַפָּרָשָׁה מְבָאֶרֶת לָנוּ כָּל הַשָּׁלֹשׁ נְקֻדּוֹת הַנַּ"ל, כִּי וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה וְכוּ', זֶה בְּחִינַת נְקֻדָּה הַכְּלָלִיּוּת. כִּי מֹשֶׁה הוּא בְּחִינַת נְקֻדָּה הַכְּלָלִיּוּת, כְּמוֹ שֶׁמְּבֹאָר שָׁם עַל פָּסוּק, אֵלֶּה הַדְּבָרִים אֲשֶׁר תְּדַבֵּר וְכוּ'. וְזֶהוּ, וְהָיוּ הַדְּבָרִים הָאֵלֶּה אֲשֶׁר אָנֹכִי מְצַוְּךָ הַיּוֹם עַל לְבָבֶךָ, הַיְנוּ שֶׁתָּאִיר וּתְקַשֵּׁר הַדִּבּוּרִים שֶׁל בְּחִינַת מֹשֶׁה שֶׁהוּא נְקֻדָּה הַכְּלָלִיּוּת עַל לְבָבֶךָ לְהָאִיר הַנְּקֻדָּה הַכְּלָלִיּוּת לְתוֹךְ הַלֵּב. וְשִׁנַּנְתָּם לְבָנֶיךָ זֶה בְּחִינַת נְקֻדָּה הַשְּׁנִיָּה, בְּחִינַת נְקֻדַּת הַחֲבֵרִים שֶׁמְּקַבְּלִין דֵּין מִן דֵּין, כְּמוֹ שֶׁמְּבֹאָר לְעֵיל שֶׁהַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁמֵּאִיר לְבָנָיו הִוא בְּחִינַת נְקֻדַּת הַחֲבֵרִים כַּנַּ"ל. 'וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם' וְכוּ', זֶה בְּחִינַת נְקֻדָּה הַשְּׁלִישִׁית שֶׁצְּרִיכִין לְהָאִיר מִנֵּהּ וּבֵהּ. וְזֶהוּ, וְדִבַּרְתָּ בָּם שֶׁצְּרִיכִין לְדַבֵּר גַּם בְּעַצְמוֹ כְּדֵי לְהָאִיר הַנְּקֻדָּה מִנֵּהּ וּבֵהּ כַּנַּ"ל. נִמְצָא, שֶׁמְּבֹאָר בְּפָרָשַׁת קְרִיאַת שְׁמַע כָּל הַשָּׁלֹשׁ נְקֻדּוֹת הַנַּ"ל, כִּי קְרִיאַת שְׁמַע הִיא בְּחִינַת אוֹר הַנְּקֻדָּה שֶׁהִיא עֶצֶם הַקְּדֻשָּׁה שֶׁהִיא הָאֱמוּנָה, כִּי עִקַּר הַקְּדֻשָּׁה הִיא הָאֱמוּנָה כַּנַּ"ל:</div>

<p class="first">And this is the aspect of <strong><em>Kri'as Shema</em></strong>. <span class="verse-inline">"Shema Yisrael, Hashem Elokeinu, Hashem Echad"</span> — this is the aspect of the light of the holy <em>nekudah</em> that is in every single Jew. For the primary holiness of the <em>nekudah</em> is the <strong>holy <em>emunah</em></strong>, which is the foundation of everything. For <em>emunah</em> is the primary <em>kedushah</em>, the generality of the entire Torah, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"All Your <em>mitzvos</em> are <em>emunah</em>"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Psalms 119:86)</span>. And it is the primary <em>nekudah</em> of the aspect of <em>tzadik</em>, as it is written, <span class="verse-inline">"And a <em>tzadik</em> lives by his <em>emunah</em>"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Habakkuk 2:4)</span>.</p>

<p>And we must say <em>Kri'as Shema</em> with a full mouth specifically — for the primary light of the <em>nekudah</em> is revealed through speech of the mouth specifically, as mentioned above. And this is: <span class="verse-inline">"And you shall love Hashem your G-d"</span> etc. <em>"V'ahavta"</em> — this is the aspect of the light of the holy love that rests near the <em>nekudah</em>, as mentioned above. And this is: <span class="verse-inline">"And these words that I command you today shall be upon your heart"</span> <span class="verse-source">(Deuteronomy 6:6)</span>. <em>"Upon your heart"</em> specifically — for one must bind and illuminate the <em>nekudah</em> from the mouth to the heart, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>And the <em>parashah</em> explains to us all <strong>three <em>nekudos</em></strong>: <span class="verse-inline">"And these words that I command you"</span> etc. — this is the aspect of the all-inclusive <em>nekudah</em>. For Moshe is the aspect of the all-inclusive <em>nekudah</em>, as is explained there on the verse <span class="verse-inline">"These are the words that you shall speak"</span> etc. And this is: <span class="verse-inline">"And these words that I command you today shall be upon your heart"</span> — that is, you shall illuminate and bind the words of the aspect of Moshe, who is the all-inclusive <em>nekudah</em>, upon your heart, to illuminate the all-inclusive <em>nekudah</em> into the heart. <span class="verse-inline">"And you shall teach them to your sons (<em>v'shinantam l'vanecha</em>)"</span> — this is the aspect of the <strong>second <em>nekudah</em></strong>, the aspect of the <em>nekudas hachaveirim</em>, who receive one from another — as is explained above, that the <em>nekudah</em> that one illuminates to his sons is the aspect of the <em>nekudas hachaveirim</em>, as mentioned above. <span class="verse-inline">"And you shall speak of them (<em>v'dibarta bam</em>)"</span> etc. — this is the aspect of the <strong>third <em>nekudah</em></strong>: one must illuminate from within oneself (<em>minei u'vei</em>). And this is <span class="verse-inline">"and you shall speak of them"</span> — one must also speak by oneself, in order to illuminate the <em>nekudah</em> from within oneself, as mentioned above.</p>

<p>It turns out that explained in the <em>parashah</em> of <em>Kri'as Shema</em> are all three aforementioned <em>nekudos</em>. For <em>Kri'as Shema</em> is the aspect of the light of the <em>nekudah</em>, which is the essence of <em>kedushah</em>, which is <em>emunah</em> — for the primary <em>kedushah</em> is <em>emunah</em>, as mentioned above.</p>

